pha1  From the jwt handler in version v1beta1 to the new configuration of the jwt handler in version v2alpha1    The migration procedure from OAuth2 handlers based on Ory Oathkeeper to the new extAuth handler will be published in the next blog post. For now, see the tutorial Exposing a Workload with extAuth.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-03\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2034 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Australia (Sydney)\nDescription: Australia (Sydney) (cf-ap30) is available as a new region running on Google Cloud for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2035 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Brazil (São Paulo)\nDescription: Brazil (São Paulo) (cf-br20) is available as a new region running on Azure for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2036 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center Improvements\nDescription: The following improvements are introduced for the SAP Task Center Web app:    Handling of attachments with IDs that include special characters      Support for opening task directly via deep links    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2037 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Ver